From 195952bbd60793c7675ffebc05a891e2d52be709 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Techniix <Techniix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:12:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nvkmd/nvrm: say what the GPU is doing when a CPU wait stalls

A CPU wait that stalls (patch 0006) printed only the sync's own counters,
e.g. "timeline wait_value 13: value 11 submit_seq 13". That cannot tell
apart a channel parked on a semaphore acquire, a channel stopped by an
RC error (a GPU fault: NVK never checked during CPU waits, so the wait
just spun forever), or releases that executed out of order and left a
lower payload behind.

- Each channel keeps a small log of the host semaphore acquires and
  releases it emitted (GPU address, value, and the fence of the submit
  cycle carrying them), written under sync_mutex.
- The stalled-wait report now also prints each wait's GPU address and,
  on the first report and every 30 s after, every registered channel:
  completed vs submitted fence, GPGet/GPPut, RC error status, every
  acquire not yet completed with the payload's current value and whether
  it is satisfied, and the latest releases.
  The payload is only read for methods the channel hasn't completed:
  pool pages live until device teardown and freed sync memory is retired
  only after the channel's work (patch 0008), and both reclaim and the
  report run under sync_mutex.
- A CPU wait now fails with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, after printing the
  channel's state, when any channel of the device has an RC error,
  instead of waiting forever on work that can no longer complete.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVRp8kiTtm6UwGrx2GPsdP
